# Mobile image loading

When navigating from a painted list/grid/row into a detail header that shows the same artwork:

## Do

- Pass **preview** params (`previewImageUrl`, `previewTitle`) from the source when the row already
  has them — use `podcastDetailParams` (or the matching helper for other entity types).
- Seed the detail header from those params **synchronously** on first paint; refresh from the DTO
  when it arrives. Hydrate from SQLite when preview is missing and a local row exists.
- Render all product artwork through **`CoverImage`** (`expo-image`, memory+disk cache).
- Use the **same list-size URL** on list and compact header so the cache hits
  (**header-hero-image-sources**).

## Don't

- Don't navigate with only an id when the source already painted a title and image — that produces
  the placeholder cover until the network returns.
- Don't `await` prefetch (or any image warm-up) before `navigation.navigate`.
- Don't show the `CoverImage` placeholder when a URI is already known from preview or local store.
- Don't prefetch lightbox / largest-original URLs on list tap.

Section chips that appear only after a detail DTO (Official Clips, Podroll, episode chapters,
and the like) follow the same first-paint habit via the **device chrome cache**, not extra
list-API fields — **mobile-section-chrome-cache**.

Subscribe, the notification bell, and download/delete icons follow the same habit —
**mobile-navigate-known-state**. Pass what the source already knows; do not default and correct.

